{"ocrText": "the Hall but there were no develop-\nments. They then decided to \" get\nout quick.\" On reaching home, David\ntold his father and they returned to the\nspot by car, but nothing was to be seen.\nThe object had emitted a humming\nsound and its brightness was compared\nto that of the Moon on a dim night.\n***\nSeaton Burn Black Ovals\n;:::i:--^6s\nThough now somewhat dated, this re-\nport of an incident in June 1973 has\njust come to hand and is, I think,\nsufficiently unusual to justify inclusion:\nIan Drever, Graham Dobson and\nothers were talking in the schoolyard\nat Wideopen, Seaton Burn, Newcastle-\nupon-Tyne, when they spotted a black\nobject in the sky giving off a smoke\ntrail. Ian ran over to a group of\npeople to make them look so as to have\nmore witnesses and they watched the\nobject fly down over Seaton Burn.\nThen, four other objects were seen\napparently 'homing in' on Seaton\nBurn: these were flying in from various\ndirections and the first object now\njoined them and they all flew together\nin a figure eight formation. They\nbegan to fly closer together and the\nfigure of eight became smaller, then\nthey suddenly turned towards the\nsame point in space and vanished. All\nt4\nhad been emitting black smoke trails\nand these vanished about one minute\nafter the objects disappeared. The\ntime was 12.45 inthe afternoon and the\nobjects-all black sharply-defined ovals\nhad been in view for between one and\nthree minutes.\n***\nAnglesey again\nReaders will remember the daylight\nsighting by pupils and their teacher at\nRhos-y-bol school in Anglesey re-\nported in Vol 6, No 1. At the end of\nOctober I received a letter from Police\nConstable John Owen of Bodorgan,\nAnglesey, telling me of an object seen\nboth by his wife and himself on Friday,\n21 October 1977 at 12.50 am. Now\n37, he has been a constable for 19 years.\ntt Thin red-coloured flame \"\nHe wrote: \"\nAt the pafticular\ntime my wife was preparing for bed\nand awaiting my arrival home. Before\nretiring, she decided to draw back the\ncuftains in the back kitchen-the\nwindow looks out towards the sandy\nAberffraw Common. On looking out\n. . . . she saw a long thing red-coloured\nflame in the sky. This flame appeared\nto be vibrating, but did not seem to be\nmoving in any particular direction.\nAt first my wife thought it was an air-\ncraft on fire, but within seconds the\n' flame' appeared to form a circle and a\ndomed figure appeared. This figure\nthen started going backwards and\nforwards. There was no mistaking the\nshape and such things as portholes\ncould be seen quite plainly.\n\" At this time I arrived home by car\nand my wife came running into the\ngarage: to say that she was excited\nwould be putting it mildly. She was\nable to say what she had seen and\nadded that it was still there. I rushed\nI\nI\nI\nII", "textLayer": [{"text": "the", "x": 6.79, "y": 4.7, "w": 3.56, "h": 2.07, "fontSize": 11.0}, {"text": "Hall but", "x": 10.47, "y": 4.63, "w": 8.28, "h": 2.17, "fontSize": 11.5}, {"text": "there", "x": 18.85, "y": 4.78, "w": 5.21, "h": 1.98, "fontSize": 10.5}, {"text": "were", "x": 24.1, "y": 4.85, "w": 4.74, "h": 1.89, "fontSize": 10.0}, {"text": "no", "x": 29.04, "y": 4.7, "w": 2.96, "h": 2.07, "fontSize": 11.0}, {"text": "develop-", "x": 32.15, "y": 5.0, "w": 6.69, "h": 1.7, "fontSize": 9.0}, {"text": "ments. They", "x": 6.79, "y": 5.98, "w": 13.07, "h": 2.17, "fontSize": 11.5}, {"text": "then", "x": 19.92, "y": 6.05, "w": 4.74, "h": 2.07, "fontSize": 11.0}, {"text": "decided", "x": 24.9, "y": 6.2, "w": 7.33, "h": 1.89, "fontSize": 10.0}, {"text": "to", "x": 32.43, "y": 5.68, "w": 2.91, "h": 2.55, "fontSize": 13.5}, {"text": "\"", "x": 35.41, "y": 6.16, "w": 1.29, "h": 1.98, "fontSize": 10.5}, {"text": "get", "x": 36.81, "y": 6.36, "w": 2.29, "h": 1.6, "fontSize": 8.5}, {"text": "out", "x": 6.79, "y": 7.69, "w": 3.07, "h": 1.79, "fontSize": 9.5}, {"text": "quick.\"", "x": 9.96, "y": 7.22, "w": 7.55, "h": 2.26, "fontSize": 12.0}, {"t